#!/usr/bin/env python3
"""verdict-incremental — after a red full run, rerun only what the fix can have changed.

    verdict-incremental plan   <root> [--full] [--tree <t>] [--out <file>]
    verdict-incremental record <root> --results <file> --rc <n> --elapsed <s> [--tree <t> --commit <c>] [--base-tree <b>]
    verdict-incremental chain  <common-dir> <tree>

WHY. The 0.3.7 train ran `setup/verify-for-push` six times in about five hours
(measured 2026-10-07: 870-3879 s each). Every fix changes the tree, the verdict
cached for the old tree stops applying, and fixing ONE test paid the WHOLE suite
again. A full run already knows, per job, what passed and what failed; a fix
that touches three files cannot have turned a subject that never names them.

THE RECORD. A FULL run (every job, `HW_TEST_ONLY` unset) leaves
`<common-dir>/hw-push-verified/<tree>.subjects` whether it was green or red:
the tree, the commit, and one `ok|red` row per job, as setup/test-hw judged it
(`HW_TEST_RESULTS`). The name is not 40 hex, so every reader of that directory
that looks for a tree verdict skips it (pre-push, bin/hw, release/cut).

THE PLAN. For HEAD's tree T2 it picks the recorded full run T1 whose tree differs
least, and reruns ONLY:

  · the jobs red in T1;
  · what setup/gate-select says the changed paths reach — the fast subjects,
    the `# gate-reference:` goldens, the changed subject files themselves, and
    EVERY slow subject `touched` names (its budget cut is the pre-commit's
    economy; this is the full run, so nothing is cut);
  · the subjects that carry a mutant anchored on a changed file
    (setup/mutation-anchors.tsv);
  · the guard jobs, when a guard changed;
  · any job T1 never ran (a new subject);
  · of the in-process suite (setup/go-test-core.sh), only the partitions the fast gate's own map says the diff
    reaches, the ones red in T1 and the ones T1 never ran (`go-test-core.sh:<partition>` lines of the job list,
    `go-test-core.sh:-` for none); every other partition keeps the row it had. Without that map it queues them all.

If all of them pass, verify-for-push caches a FULL verdict for T2 that names T1
(`base_tree=`, `incremental=1`, `chain_depth=`) AND leaves T2's own record, so the
next tree can start from T2 instead of paying a new full run (2026-10-14: every
merge after the brainer's full run forced another 2h30 once the diff to that run
passed the caps that existed then: they are gone, see below). A record is either a
real full run (depth 0) or a green incremental one whose rows are its base's, overlaid by the jobs it re-ran
(`kind=incremental`, `base_tree=`, `root_tree=` the real full run, `chain_depth=`
hops from it). THE CHAIN IS CAPPED at HW_VERDICT_MAX_CHAIN hops (3): a hop onto an
incremental verdict compounds gate-select's one blind spot (a path built at
runtime names nothing) — a job a diff reached only that way keeps the row it had
— and the cap is what bounds how many diffs can hide behind one full run. A
record at the cap is no base: the plan starts from the nearest record that is,
the real full run, and gate-selects the WHOLE diff since it (2026-10-16: it used to
become a full run, 2h30 for a diff gate-select can answer). The release cut stays
at ONE hop (`chain`): a release claims "the whole suite passed on these bytes".

IT FALLS BACK TO A FULL RUN, saying why, when any of these holds:

  · `--full` (or HW_VERDICT_FULL=1);
  · no usable record (none at all, or every one at the hop cap or with a red that
    belongs to no job);
  · the diff touches the runner or anything it loads — the list is READ from
    setup/test-hw (every `$HERE/<file>` and `$SOURCE_ROOT/<file>` it names,
    plus what those scripts source), not kept by hand — or anything under
    setup/tests/ that is not a subject (_common.sh, lib*);
  · gate-select FAILS (an error is not an answer).

A path gate-select cannot map (`all`: built at runtime, named by no fast
subject) is NOT a fall back: the pre-commit already answers it with the whole
FAST gate, and so does this, plus every slow subject `touched` names. Measured
on 20 sampled commits, 7 answered `all`, mostly a bin/ script only slow
subjects name; falling back to the full suite for those would leave most fixes
paying it. The blind spot is gate-select's own and is the same one the fast gate
carries; the full run it feeds is still a full run for every job it did not skip.

SIZE IS NOT A REASON (2026-10-16). It used to fall back to a full run for more than
30 files, more than 25 commits from the base, or a chain past 3 hops. The first two
guarded gate-select's over-selection, which only makes the plan run more, never less;
the third is the base choice above. A big diff gets a big incremental plan: the whole
fast gate plus what the diff names, which still costs less than the full suite, and
the blind spot is the same one every incremental plan carries.

A fall back is the old behaviour exactly. Nothing here can cache a verdict
cheaper than the full run's unless every named job passed.
"""
import fnmatch
import hashlib
import importlib.machinery
import importlib.util
import os
import re
import subprocess
import sys
import tempfile
import time

# gate-select is IMPORTED below; a .pyc beside it would be an untracked file in the checkout.
sys.dont_write_bytecode = True
MAX_CHAIN = int(os.environ.get("HW_VERDICT_MAX_CHAIN", "3"))
HEX40 = re.compile(r"^[0-9a-f]{40}$")
GUARD_JOBS = ("test-deny-repo-writes.mjs", "test-deny-repo-writes-filesystem.mjs",
              "test-opencode-hw-blocked-reason.mjs", "test-herdr-opencode-background-state.mjs",
              "mutate-deny-repo-writes.sh")
# Named by the brief, in case the runner's own text stops naming them.
EXTRA_SHARED = ("setup/verify-for-push", "setup/verdict-incremental", "setup/release/cut",
                "guards.json", "bin/hw-test*")


def git(root, *args, check=True):
    r = subprocess.run(["git", "-C", root, "-c", "core.quotepath=off", *args],
                       capture_output=True, text=True,
                       env={k: v for k, v in os.environ.items() if not k.startswith("GIT_")})
    if check and r.returncode != 0:
        raise RuntimeError("git %s: %s" % (" ".join(args), r.stderr.strip()))
    return r


def common_dir(root):
    c = git(root, "rev-parse", "--git-common-dir").stdout.strip()
    return c if os.path.isabs(c) else os.path.join(root, c)


def read(path):
    try:
        with open(path, encoding="utf-8", errors="replace") as fh:
            return fh.read()
    except OSError:
        return ""


# ── what the runner loads: read from it, never kept by hand ───────────────────

def runner_files(root):
    """Repo-relative paths the runner names or sources; globs allowed."""
    found = {"setup/test-hw"}
    text = re.sub(r"(?m)^\s*#.*$", "", read(os.path.join(root, "setup", "test-hw")))
    todo = []
    for m in re.finditer(r"\$\{?(HERE|SOURCE_ROOT)\}?/([A-Za-z0-9_./-]+)", text):
        base = "setup" if m.group(1) == "HERE" else ""
        rel = os.path.normpath(os.path.join(base, m.group(2)))
        if rel.startswith(".."):
            continue
        todo.append(rel)
    for m in re.finditer(r"\$HERE/\.\./([A-Za-z0-9_./-]+)", text):
        todo.append(os.path.normpath(m.group(1)))
    seen = set()
    while todo:
        rel = todo.pop()
        if rel in seen:
            continue
        seen.add(rel)
        full = os.path.join(root, rel)
        # Directories the runner walks are not files it loads: guards/ and
        # tests/ are handled by what a job IS (a guard job, a subject).
        if not os.path.isfile(full):
            continue
        found.add(rel)
        # One level of what a loaded script sources: `. "$HERE/x"`, `source x`.
        for sm in re.finditer(r"(?m)^\s*(?:\.|source)\s+[\"']?[^\s\"';]*?([A-Za-z0-9_-]+\.sh)\b",
                              re.sub(r"(?m)^\s*#.*$", "", read(full))):
            for d in ("setup", "bin", "setup/tests"):
                cand = os.path.join(d, sm.group(1))
                if os.path.isfile(os.path.join(root, cand)) and cand not in seen:
                    todo.append(cand)
    found.discard("setup/guards")
    # The guard drivers and mutation arm are JOBS, selected by what they are.
    return {f for f in found if not f.startswith("setup/guards/") and not f.startswith("setup/tests/[")}


# A `# MUTATION-ANCHOR: <id>` (or -END) comment closing a line, alone or several in a row. It is a
# declaration read by setup/mutation-anchors.tsv and 540, never code: no subject's verdict moves with it.
ANCHOR_TAIL = re.compile(r"(?:[ \t]*#[ \t]*MUTATION-ANCHOR(?:-END)?:[ \t]*[A-Za-z0-9][\w.-]*)+[ \t]*$")  # MUTATION-ANCHOR: 820-M04


# 540 judges every marker against setup/mutation-anchors.tsv, but its gate-when matches no runner path:
# a marker-only runner change is trusted by the strip above, so the job that checks the markers is forced.
ANCHOR_JOB = "540-las-anclas-de-mutacion-existen.sh"


def without_anchor_markers(text):
    out = []
    for line in text.split("\n"):
        stripped = ANCHOR_TAIL.sub("", line)  # MUTATION-ANCHOR: 820-M05
        if stripped != line and not stripped.strip():
            continue  # a whole-line marker
        out.append(stripped)
    return "\n".join(out)


def only_anchor_markers_changed(root, base, tree, path):
    """True when the file differs between the two trees ONLY by anchor markers. Anything else, a file
    that is new or gone, or a git that cannot say, is False: the caller falls back to a full run."""
    old = git(root, "show", "%s:%s" % (base, path), check=False)
    new = git(root, "show", "%s:%s" % (tree, path), check=False)
    if old.returncode != 0 or new.returncode != 0:
        return False
    return without_anchor_markers(old.stdout) == without_anchor_markers(new.stdout)


def is_runner_path(path, shared):
    if path in shared:
        return True
    if any(fnmatch.fnmatch(path, g) for g in shared if "*" in g):
        return True
    if path.startswith("setup/tests/") and not re.match(r"^setup/tests/[0-9]+-[^/]*\.sh$", path):
        return True  # _common.sh, lib*, fixtures: every subject can read them
    return False


# ── records ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

def parse_record(path):
    head, rows = {}, {}
    text = read(path)
    if not text:
        return None
    part = text.split("\n\n", 1)
    for line in part[0].split("\n"):
        if "=" in line:
            k, v = line.split("=", 1)
            head[k] = v
    for line in (part[1] if len(part) > 1 else "").split("\n"):
        f = line.split("\t")
        if len(f) == 3 and f[2] in ("ok", "red"):
            rows[f[0]] = (f[1], f[2])
    return {"head": head, "rows": rows}


def record_depth(h):
    """Hops from a real full run: 0 for one, else the record's chain_depth (-1 when it is not a number)."""
    if h.get("kind") == "full":
        return 0
    d = h.get("chain_depth", "")
    return int(d) if d.isdigit() else -1


def current_impl():
    """The implementation this run measures: HW_IMPL=bash is the rollback, anything else is the Go default."""
    return "bash" if os.environ.get("HW_IMPL", "go") == "bash" else "go"


def usable_base(path, tree_from_name, chain=False):
    """A record a plan may start from: a real full run, and with chain=True also a green incremental one
    still under the hop cap (a new run off it would be at most MAX_CHAIN hops from the full run)."""
    rec = parse_record(path)
    if not rec:
        return None, "unreadable"
    h = rec["head"]
    if (h.get("impl") or "go") != current_impl():
        # A record is rows of jobs as ONE implementation judged them; a plan under the other would vouch for rows it never ran.
        return None, "it measured impl=%s, this run is impl=%s" % (h.get("impl") or "go", current_impl())
    if h.get("kind") != "full":
        if not chain or h.get("kind") != "incremental":
            return None, "not a full run"
        depth = record_depth(h)
        if depth < 1 or not HEX40.match(h.get("root_tree", "")) or not HEX40.match(h.get("base_tree", "")):
            return None, "an incremental record that does not name its chain"
        if depth >= MAX_CHAIN:  # MUTATION-ANCHOR: 820-M08
            return None, "its chain is %d hops from a full run, at the cap of %d" % (depth, MAX_CHAIN)
    if h.get("tree") != tree_from_name or not HEX40.match(tree_from_name):
        return None, "names another tree"
    if h.get("runner_red") != "0":
        return None, "its run had a red that belongs to no job"
    if not rec["rows"]:
        return None, "no job rows"
    return rec, ""


def write_atomic(path, text):
    tmp = "%s.tmp.%d" % (path, os.getpid())
    with open(tmp, "w", encoding="utf-8") as fh:
        fh.write(text)
    os.replace(tmp, path)


def cmd_record(root, results, rc, elapsed, tree=None, commit=None, base_tree=None):
    # THE TREE THAT WAS TESTED, not the one HEAD points to when the run ends: a
    # full run lasts ~1000 s over a snapshot taken at its start, and another
    # agent committing into the shared tree meanwhile moves HEAD. Filing the
    # results under that later tree would hand the next plan a base whose diff
    # is near-empty and whose rows describe other bytes. verify-for-push passes
    # what it captured before the run; without it, HEAD is the best there is.
    if tree or commit:
        if not (tree and commit and HEX40.match(tree) and HEX40.match(commit)):
            print("verdict-incremental: --tree and --commit go together and are 40-hex — no record written", file=sys.stderr)
            return 1
        r = git(root, "rev-parse", "--verify", "-q", commit + "^{tree}", check=False)
        if r.returncode != 0 or r.stdout.strip() != tree:
            print("verdict-incremental: commit %s is not tree %s — no record written" % (commit[:9], tree[:9]), file=sys.stderr)
            return 1
    else:
        tree = git(root, "rev-parse", "HEAD^{tree}").stdout.strip()
        commit = git(root, "rev-parse", "HEAD").stdout.strip()
    rows = []
    runner_red = 0
    for line in read(results).split("\n"):
        f = line.split("\t")
        if len(f) != 3 or f[2] not in ("ok", "red"):
            continue
        if f[0] == "runner":
            runner_red = 1
            continue
        rows.append(f)
    if not rows:
        print("verdict-incremental: %s has no job rows — no record written" % results, file=sys.stderr)
        return 1
    reds = sum(1 for r in rows if r[2] == "red")
    # A non-zero run with no red JOB is red for a reason no job owns.
    if int(rc) != 0 and reds == 0:
        runner_red = 1
    d = os.path.join(common_dir(root), "hw-push-verified")
    os.makedirs(d, exist_ok=True)
    kind, extra = "full", []
    if base_tree:
        # AN INCREMENTAL RUN'S RECORD: only a GREEN one is a base (a red leaves nothing to stand on), made of
        # its base's rows with the jobs this run re-ran written over them.
        if int(rc) != 0 or reds or runner_red:
            print("verdict-incremental: a red incremental run is no base — no record written", file=sys.stderr)
            return 1
        if base_tree == tree:  # MUTATION-ANCHOR: 820-M10
            # A red full run re-run on the SAME tree is its own nearest base: its record is the real full run
            # `chain` and the release cut stand on, and it must not be overwritten by an incremental one.
            print("verdict-incremental: the base is this very tree — its record stays, none written", file=sys.stderr)
            return 1
        brec, why = usable_base(os.path.join(d, base_tree + ".subjects"), base_tree, chain=True)
        if brec is None:
            print("verdict-incremental: base %s is not usable (%s) — no record written" % (base_tree[:9], why), file=sys.stderr)
            return 1
        merged = dict(brec["rows"])
        for r in rows:
            merged[r[0]] = (r[1], r[2])
        rows = [[n, k, st] for n, (k, st) in sorted(merged.items())]
        depth = record_depth(brec["head"]) + 1
        kind = "incremental"
        extra = ["base_tree=" + base_tree, "root_tree=" + (brec["head"].get("root_tree") or base_tree),
                 "chain_depth=%d" % depth]
    head = ["kind=" + kind, "impl=" + current_impl(), "tree=" + tree, "commit=" + commit,
            "recorded_at=" + time.strftime("%Y-%m-%dT%H:%M:%SZ", time.gmtime()),
            "elapsed_seconds=" + str(elapsed), "rc=" + str(rc), "runner_red=%d" % runner_red,
            "jobs=%d" % len(rows), "reds=%d" % reds] + extra
    body = "\n".join("\t".join(r) for r in rows)
    write_atomic(os.path.join(d, tree + ".subjects"), "\n".join(head) + "\n\n" + body + "\n")
    print("verdict-incremental: recorded %d jobs (%d red) for tree %s%s" % (len(rows), reds, tree, " (incremental, chain_depth=%d)" % depth if base_tree else ""), file=sys.stderr)
    return 0


# ── the plan ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

def load_gate_select(root):
    path = os.path.join(root, "setup", "gate-select")
    return path if os.path.isfile(path) else None


def run_gate_select(root, paths, mode=None):
    gs = load_gate_select(root)
    if gs is None:
        raise RuntimeError("setup/gate-select is absent")
    pat = ""
    lib = os.path.join(root, "setup", "hooks", "suite-trigger-pattern.sh")
    if os.path.isfile(lib):
        r = subprocess.run(["bash", "-c", '. "$1" && printf %s "${SUITE_TRIGGER_PATTERN:-}"', "_", lib],
                           capture_output=True, text=True)
        pat = r.stdout
    with tempfile.NamedTemporaryFile("w", delete=False, prefix="vi-changed.") as fh:
        fh.write("\n".join(paths) + "\n")
        name = fh.name
    try:
        args = ["python3", gs, root, name, pat] + ([mode] if mode else [])
        r = subprocess.run(args, capture_output=True, text=True)
    finally:
        os.unlink(name)
    if r.returncode != 0:
        raise RuntimeError("setup/gate-select failed (exit %d): %s" % (r.returncode, (r.stderr or r.stdout).strip().split("\n")[-1]))
    return [l for l in r.stdout.split("\n") if l.strip()]


def gate_select_module(root):
    gs = load_gate_select(root)
    if gs is None:
        return None
    loader = importlib.machinery.SourceFileLoader("vi_gate_select", gs)
    spec = importlib.util.spec_from_loader("vi_gate_select", loader)
    mod = importlib.util.module_from_spec(spec)
    try:
        loader.exec_module(mod)
    except Exception:
        return None
    return mod


def is_guard_path(root, path):
    """The guard drivers' own definition (gate-select's GUARD), else the directory."""
    mod = gate_select_module(root)
    if mod is not None and hasattr(mod, "GUARD"):
        return mod.GUARD.search(path) is not None
    return path.startswith("setup/guards/")


def fast_subjects(root, tests):
    """Every subject setup/test-budgets.json classifies fast (what the fast gate runs)."""
    import json
    try:
        b = json.loads(read(os.path.join(root, "setup", "test-budgets.json")))
        thr = b["fast_gate_threshold_seconds"]
        return sorted(n for n, v in b["files"].items() if v["seconds"] <= thr and n in tests)
    except (ValueError, KeyError, TypeError):
        return list(tests)  # unreadable budgets: every subject is the safe answer


def anchored_subjects(root, changed, tests):
    """Subjects whose mutants are anchored on a changed file: `<N>-Mxx<TAB><file>`."""
    out = {}
    for line in read(os.path.join(root, "setup", "mutation-anchors.tsv")).split("\n"):
        f = line.split("\t")
        if len(f) < 2 or f[1] not in changed:
            continue
        n = f[0].split("-M")[0]
        hit = [x for x in tests if re.match(r"^%s-" % re.escape(n), x)]
        for x in hit:
            out.setdefault(x, "a mutant anchored on %s" % f[1])
    return out


def go_partitions(root, changed, rows):
    """-> ({partition: why} to run, [every partition]) for the in-process suite (setup/go-test-core.sh), or (None, [])
    when it cannot say, which leaves the whole suite queued as before.

    A partition runs when the fast gate's own map says the diff can have moved it (`go-test-core.sh --affected`: what each
    partition READS, measured, and everything for a path nobody measured), when the recorded run had it red, or when the
    recorded run never ran it (no row, or a row named by another job shape)."""
    script = os.path.join(root, "setup", "go-test-core.sh")
    if not os.path.isfile(script) or not os.path.isfile(os.path.join(root, "core", "go.mod")):
        return None, []
    env = {k: v for k, v in os.environ.items() if not k.startswith("GIT_")}
    r = subprocess.run(["bash", script, "--list"], capture_output=True, text=True, cwd=root, env=env)
    names = [l.split("\t")[0] for l in r.stdout.split("\n") if l.strip()]
    if r.returncode != 0 or not names:
        return None, []
    with tempfile.NamedTemporaryFile("w", delete=False, prefix="vi-go-changed.") as fh:
        fh.write("\n".join(changed) + "\n")
        name = fh.name
    try:
        a = subprocess.run(["bash", script, "--affected", name], capture_output=True, text=True, cwd=root, env=env)
    finally:
        os.unlink(name)
    if a.returncode != 0:
        return None, []
    affected = set(a.stdout.split())
    sel = {}
    for n in names:
        row = rows.get("go-test-core.sh:" + n)
        if n in affected:
            sel[n] = "go-test-core.sh --affected <- the diff"
        elif row is None:
            sel[n] = "a partition the recorded run never ran"
        elif row[1] == "red":
            sel[n] = "red in the recorded run"  # MUTATION-ANCHOR: 1090-M05
    return sel, names


def cmd_plan(root, full, out, expect_tree=None):
    def fallback(why):
        print("full %s" % why)
        return 0

    if full or os.environ.get("HW_VERDICT_FULL"):
        return fallback("--full was asked for")
    try:
        tree = git(root, "rev-parse", "HEAD^{tree}").stdout.strip()
        d = os.path.join(common_dir(root), "hw-push-verified")
    except RuntimeError as e:
        return fallback("could not read the repository (%s)" % e)
    if expect_tree and expect_tree != tree:
        return fallback("HEAD's tree is %s, not the %s the caller captured: the checkout moved" % (tree[:9], expect_tree[:9]))
    tests_dir = os.path.join(root, "setup", "tests")
    tests = sorted(x for x in os.listdir(tests_dir) if re.match(r"^[0-9]+-.*\.sh$", x)) if os.path.isdir(tests_dir) else []
    if not tests:
        return fallback("no subject files found")
    shared = set(EXTRA_SHARED) | runner_files(root)

    best = None
    skipped = []
    for fn in sorted(os.listdir(d)) if os.path.isdir(d) else []:
        if not fn.endswith(".subjects"):
            continue
        base = fn[:-len(".subjects")]
        rec, why = usable_base(os.path.join(d, fn), base, chain=True)  # MUTATION-ANCHOR: 820-M09
        if rec is None:
            skipped.append("%s (%s)" % (base[:9], why))
            continue
        if git(root, "cat-file", "-e", base + "^{tree}", check=False).returncode != 0:
            skipped.append("%s (tree is not in this repository)" % base[:9])
            continue
        r = git(root, "diff", "--name-only", "--no-renames", "-z", base, tree, check=False)
        if r.returncode != 0:
            skipped.append("%s (diff failed)" % base[:9])
            continue
        files = [x for x in r.stdout.split("\0") if x]
        commit = rec["head"].get("commit", "")
        dist = None
        if HEX40.match(commit) and git(root, "cat-file", "-e", commit + "^{commit}", check=False).returncode == 0:
            c = git(root, "rev-list", "--count", commit + "...HEAD", check=False)
            if c.returncode == 0 and c.stdout.strip().isdigit():
                dist = int(c.stdout.strip())
        key = (len(files), dist if dist is not None else 10 ** 9)
        if best is None or key < best[0]:
            best = (key, base, rec, files, dist)
    if best is None:
        return fallback("no recorded full run to start from%s" % (" (skipped: %s)" % ", ".join(skipped[:3]) if skipped else ""))
    _, base, rec, changed, dist = best  # MUTATION-ANCHOR: 820-M11
    if dist is None:
        return fallback("the recorded run %s names a commit this repository does not have, so its distance is unknown" % base[:9])
    marked = set()  # runner paths changed only by anchor markers: not code, so not a reason for a full run
    for p in changed:
        if not is_runner_path(p, shared):
            continue
        if only_anchor_markers_changed(root, base, tree, p):
            marked.add(p)
            continue
        return fallback("%s is the runner or something it loads: any verdict can move" % p)  # MUTATION-ANCHOR: 820-M02

    run = {}  # name -> why

    def add(name, why):
        run.setdefault(name, why)

    if marked:
        add(ANCHOR_JOB, "a runner file changed only by anchor markers (%s): 540 checks them" % ", ".join(sorted(marked)))  # MUTATION-ANCHOR: 820-M06

    rows = rec["rows"]
    for name, (_k, st) in sorted(rows.items()):
        if st == "red":
            add(name, "red in the recorded run %s" % base[:9])
    try:
        # gate-select reads a runner path as `all` (the whole fast gate): a marker-only one is no change to it.
        code_changed = [p for p in changed if p not in marked]
        sel = run_gate_select(root, code_changed) if code_changed else []
        tch = run_gate_select(root, code_changed, "touched") if code_changed else []
    except RuntimeError as e:
        return fallback(str(e))
    guards_changed = False
    for line in sel:
        f = line.split(None, 2)
        if f[0] == "all":
            for name in fast_subjects(root, tests):
                add(name, "gate-select cannot map the diff (%s): the whole fast gate" % (f[1] if len(f) > 1 else ""))
        elif f[0] in ("core", "subject", "reference", "deferred") and len(f) > 1:
            add(f[1], "gate-select %s%s" % (f[0], " <- " + f[2] if len(f) > 2 else ""))
        elif f[0] == "guards":
            guards_changed = True
    for line in tch:  # MUTATION-ANCHOR: 820-M01
        f = line.split(None, 3)
        if f[0] in ("touched", "touched-skipped") and len(f) > 1:
            add(f[1], "gate-select touched <- %s" % f[-1])
    for name, why in anchored_subjects(root, set(changed), tests).items():
        add(name, why)
    if guards_changed or any(is_guard_path(root, p) for p in changed):
        for g in GUARD_JOBS:
            add(g, "a guard changed")
    for x in tests:
        if x not in rows:
            add(x, "a job the recorded run never ran")
    present = set(tests) | set(GUARD_JOBS)
    run = {k: v for k, v in run.items() if k in present}
    total = len(present)
    go_sel, go_all = go_partitions(root, changed, rows)  # MUTATION-ANCHOR: 1090-M03
    if not run and not go_sel:
        return fallback("nothing selected — refusing an empty run")

    parts = " partitions=%d of %d" % (len(go_sel), len(go_all)) if go_sel is not None else ""
    print("incremental base_tree=%s base_commit=%s files=%d commits=%d jobs=%d of %d%s chain_depth=%d"
          % (base, rec["head"].get("commit", ""), len(changed), dist, len(run), total, parts, record_depth(rec["head"]) + 1))
    for name in sorted(run):
        print("run %s %s" % (name, run[name]))
    lines = sorted(run)
    if go_sel is not None:
        for n in sorted(go_sel):
            print("run go-test-core.sh:%s %s" % (n, go_sel[n]))
        # `go-test-core.sh:-` is the positive "none": no line at all would leave the whole in-process suite queued
        lines += ["go-test-core.sh:" + n for n in sorted(go_sel)] or ["go-test-core.sh:-"]  # MUTATION-ANCHOR: 1090-M04
    if out:
        write_atomic(out, "\n".join(lines) + "\n")
    return 0


